    "explanation": "Decision for trip TRP-02811. Both parties are told the same thing: the record shows the rider asked for the stop, so the fare she contests stands.\n\nWhat was measured. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02811) ran 26.39 km against a 20.3 km platform optimal, an excess of 6.09 km, or 30.0%. The trace is clean for policy purposes — 100% coverage, 207 fixes at a 10-second interval, no gaps, maximum gap 0 seconds — so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and the excess is established on the trace under POL-RD-01. It is below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gate, so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no driver-conduct referral arises.\n\nWhy no refund is due. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02811) contains the rider's own message at 06:33:18 — 'can we stop at Jurong Point first, need to grab something' — sent one minute after the meter started at 06:32:18, that is before the vehicle left the optimal corridor, followed by the driver's 'ok'. The waypoint_hint the platform resolved from that message (lat 1.305461, lng 103.90726) is corroborated by the trace: the nearest fix is 21.70 m away, well inside POL-RD-04's 200 m threshold. All three conditions of POL-RD-04(a) to (c) are therefore met — the instruction was the rider's, was timely, and named a specific place — and the excess between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor, which is the detour to and from Jurong Point, is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied. With that stretch removed no excess is left to found a deviation, the driver has discharged the burden POL-RD-08 shifts to him by pointing to the chat_log and POL-RD-04, and POL-RD-01 gives NO_ACTION.\n\nThe rider's objection that this was 'a tour' is not supported. The only waypoint the trace approaches is the one the rider herself named, and the 6.09 km is the distance to it and back. The driver's statement that the rider asked for the stop is confirmed by the chat and the trace, not merely asserted.\n\nThe arithmetic offered for the rider does not issue. Charged_total was 34.00, and a recomputation against the booked 20.3 km / 27.4 min optimal would give a recomputed_fare of 27.4970, a difference of 6.5030 and a rounded 6.55. POL-RD-02 runs only against the adjusted optimal, and here the adjustment removes the whole excess, so no distance-or-time refund arises for the rider and the 0.50 de minimis question never falls to be asked.\n\nOther lines. The fare is METERED with zero ERP and toll lines, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and there is no billing-integrity referral. The rider was billed 26.4 km against a 26.39 km trace, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall and no DRIVER_COMPENSATION. Neither profile decides anything about this trip: deviation_flags_90d is 1 over 348 completed trips, below both POL-RD-06 tests, and deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the POL-RD-08 threshold; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter was flagged as context-only and is not used.\n\nTwo claims about the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02811-01, weight 0.0) were discarded by the referee for not naming the MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code and are not reinstated; in any event no party asserts an external traffic cause here, so no advisory is needed and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged.\n\nResult. The present state stands: the 34.00 charge is not refunded and no compensation is paid. The monetary effect is 0, below the 8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes on issue, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04. Confidence is 0.90, capped by the full-weight artifacts (EV-CHAT-02811, EV-GPS-02811) that carry the deciding fact."
