    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the charge for trip TRP-02811 stands. No refund is payable.\n\nWhat the record shows. The trip runs from Blk 55 Lengkok Bahru, Bukit Merah to Blk 610 Clementi West St 1. The GPS trace EV-GPS-02811 (weight 1.0; 207 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c)) records 26.39 km against the booked optimal of 20.3 km on EV-TRIP-02811 — an excess of 6.09 km, or 30.0% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests are met (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so a deviation is established on the trace.\n\nWhy it is exonerated. The chat log EV-CHAT-02811 carries the rider's own message MSG-02811-001, sent at 06:33:18 — 60 seconds after the meter started at 06:32:18, before the vehicle left the optimal corridor — reading 'can we stop at Jurong Point first, need to grab something'. The driver replied 'ok'. The message comes from the rider, is timely, and names a specific place carried by the platform as the resolved waypoint_hint (lat 1.305461, lng 103.90726). POL-RD-04 also requires the trace to corroborate the instruction, and it does: the nearest fix to that waypoint is 21.70 m away at 06:49:38, far inside the 200 m threshold. The rider asked for the stop, the driver made it, and the measured excess is the distance of that excursion out to Jurong Point and back to the booked route. POL-RD-04 excludes that excess before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied. Nothing above the POL-RD-01 thresholds remains, so no deviation survives and no refund is due. The rider's description of the trip as 'a tour' is not borne out: the only waypoint the trace approaches is the one she named, and the driver's statement that she asked for the stop is confirmed by the chat.\n\nThe money. The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not close the arithmetic route. For transparency: charged_total is 34.00, and on EV-FARE-02811 (weight 1.0) a POL-RD-02 recomputation against the booked optimal of 20.3 km / 27.4 min gives a recomputed fare of 27.4970 and an arithmetic refund of 6.5030, i.e. 6.55 payable — the figure the fare breakdown and the rider's own arithmetic claim put forward. That is not the computation that runs here, because POL-RD-04 requires it to be run against the adjusted optimal once the rider-requested excursion is excluded; on the adjusted optimal (26.39 km, duration scaled to 35.6 min) the recomputed fare is about 34.36, at or above the 34.00 charged, so the refund floors at zero. Neither the 6.55 figure nor the rider's contested 9.00 is payable, and the 90%-of-charged full-refund question therefore does not arise. The fare breakdown carries no ERP or toll lines (erp_lines.total 0.00), so POL-RD-09 pass-through corrections add nothing and no billing-integrity referral is produced.\n\nThe parties' other points. The rider bears and has discharged her initial burden under POL-RD-08: the trip identifier TRP-02811 matches across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and the excess was shown; the driver in turn pointed to a specific artifact (the chat log) and a specific clause (POL-RD-04), which shifts and discharges the burden. No repeat-deviation pattern is established — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below the 3-flag test) and 1 divided by 348 completed trips in 90 days is 0.0029 (below the 0.05 test) — so POL-RD-06 is not engaged, the 30.0% deviation is below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gate, and no driver-conduct referral issues; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only and has not been used. The rider_profile fields deviation_claims_60d (1) and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated (0) do not trigger the POL-RD-08 serial-claimant corroboration requirement, and no profile field is used to establish anything about this trip. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02811-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries nothing; no live claim relies on it, so POL-RD-03 is not in play. No driver compensation is due: the rider was billed 26.4 km against a 26.39 km trace, so there is no unbilled shortfall above 1.0 km.\n\nConfidence and effect. My confidence is 0.9. The fact this ruling turns on — that the excess is the rider-requested stop — is carried by two independent artifacts at full weight, the chat log EV-CHAT-02811 and the GPS trace EV-GPS-02811, so the cap is 1.0. The ruling is NO_ACTION: payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 are left as they are, and because the monetary effect is nil there is nothing to hold, well inside the SGD 8.00 execution threshold."
